From 9550d0808e4716bbdeb5a33b0c651d58501c038b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Emerison Six <billsix@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 03:25:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 358/488] soh: name the 20 address-named symbols defined in
 z_boss_tw.c

SoH carries the Ocarina of Time decomp, in which several thousand symbols are
still named after their ROM address. This commit names every such symbol DEFINED
IN ONE FILE, so the work can be reviewed a file at a time.

The file names the unit; it does not bound it. Each rename is applied wherever
the symbol occurs -- the declaration in the header, the definition, and every
call site -- so this commit reaches into whatever other files use these symbols
and leaves no dangling reference. It is a pure rename: no behaviour changes, and
the only edits that are not renames are the provenance comments described below.

Two name sources are used, and every name says which it came from:

  * zeldaret/oot -- SoH's decomp IS zeldaret/oot at the same ROM addresses, so
    where oot has already named a symbol, that name is adopted verbatim. The
    definition gets a "Name from zeldaret/oot" comment and every declaration a
    short "// was <addr> [oot]" tag.

  * DEDUCED -- oot leaves a great many symbols address-named too, so those
    names are inferred from the body and its callers, and are marked as OURS
    rather than passed off as upstream. The definition gets
    "LLM generated name (HIGH|GUESS), was <addr>: <reason>" and the short tag
    reads "[LLM:HIGH]" or "[LLM:GUESS]". A GUESS is tagged at every call site
    as well, not only the declaration, so a reader who meets the name anywhere
    knows it is inferred. "git grep '[LLM:'" lists every place the decomp
    leans on an inference.

The justification recorded for each individual name follows, one entry per
symbol, in the order the renames were made. Nothing is summarised away: these
are the per-commit reasons from the unsquashed history, with the boilerplate
that was identical in every one of them hoisted into the text above.

All 20 are defined in soh/src/overlays/actors/ovl_Boss_Tw/z_boss_tw.c.

  * func_80941BC0 -> BossTw_DrawIcePool
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws gTwinrovaIcePoolDL and its shine at
    groundBlastPos2

  * func_80942180 -> BossTw_DrawFirePool
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws gTwinrovaFirePoolDL with its smoke and
    flame layers at groundBlastPos2

  * func_809426F0 -> BossTw_DrawSpawnPortal
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws Kotake's or Koume's magic sigil scaled
    by spawnPortalScale, with the surrounding flames

  * func_80942C70 -> BossTw_DrawBeam
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws gTwinrovaBeamDL along
    beamOrigin/beamYaw/beamDist, plus the mirror-shield reflection segment

  * func_80943028 -> BossTw_DrawHalo
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws gTwinrovaHaloDL above the actor and its
    gCircleShadowDL ground shadow

  * func_80944C50 -> BossTw_DrawLightPillar
    deduced, confidence HIGH: draws gTwinrovaLightCircleDL,
    gTwinrovaLightRaysDL and gTwinrovaLightPillarDL

  * D_8094A7D0 -> sLaughSfxPos
    deduced, confidence HIGH: its only use is as the position argument for
    NA_SE_EN_TWINROBA_LAUGH and LAUGH2

  * D_8094C854 -> sShieldChargeAlpha
    deduced, confidence HIGH: approaches 255 while the mirror shield charges
    and 0 as it discharges; used as the prim alpha of the charge glow

  * D_8094C858 -> sShieldFlashAlpha
    deduced, confidence HIGH: prim alpha of the mirror-shield flash, driven
    up while sShieldFlashTimer runs and down after

  * D_8094C86F -> sShieldFlashTimer
    deduced, confidence HIGH: countdown that decides whether
    sShieldFlashAlpha rises or falls

  * D_8094C870 -> sShieldBlastActive
    deduced, confidence HIGH: set while a TWEFF_SHLD_BLST effect lives;
    BossTw_TwinrovaDoneBlastShoot waits for it to clear

  * D_8094C872 -> sShieldFlashScroll
    deduced, confidence HIGH: texture scroll rate of the shield flash, +7
    for the reflected beam and -7 for the charge, also selecting the 1.3x
    scale

  * D_8094C874 -> sUnusedIntroCsValue1
    deduced, confidence GUESS: written during the intro cutscene (30, 435,
    and the message index) and never read anywhere in the overlay; the name
    records that check, not an intent

  * D_8094C876 -> sUnusedIntroCsValue2
    deduced, confidence GUESS: written as 10 alongside sUnusedIntroCsValue1
    and never read

  * D_8094C878 -> sUnusedIntroCsFlag1
    deduced, confidence GUESS: set to 1 then 0 during the intro cutscene and
    never read

  * D_8094C87A -> sUnusedIntroCsValue3
    deduced, confidence GUESS: written as 335 during the intro cutscene and
    never read

  * D_8094C87C -> sUnusedIntroCsValue4
    deduced, confidence GUESS: only ever zeroed with the rest of this group;
    never written with a value and never read

  * D_8094C87E -> sUnusedIntroCsFlag2
    deduced, confidence GUESS: set to 1 during the intro cutscene and never
    read

  * D_8094A900 -> sEyeTexIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: blink table indexed by work[BLINK_IDX] to pick
    Kotake's and Koume's eye texture

  * D_8094A90C -> sTwinrovaEyeTexIndices
    deduced, confidence HIGH: the longer blink table indexed by
    work[TW_BLINK_IDX] for fused Twinrova's eyes

